{title: 198 Desciende, Espíritu de amor}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{lyricist: Isaac Watts (1674-1748); Vers; esp.:; Juan B. Cabrera (1837-1916)}
{composer: Sr; John B. Dykes, 1866 (1823-1876)}

{sov}
D[G]esciende, E[Am]spír[E7]it[Am]u d[D7]e a[G]mor,
Paloma[A7] celes[D7]tial,
[Am]promesa[A7] fiel[D7] del[G] Salva[C]dor,
[D7]de gracia manan[G]tial.

A[G]viva n[Am]uestra e[E7]sc[Am]as[D7]a f[G]e,
concédenos[A7] sa[D7]lud;
[Am]benigno[A7], guía[D7] nuestro[G] pie[C]
[D7]por sendas de vir[G]tud.

C[G]onsuela n[Am]uestro c[E7]or[Am]az[D7]ón[G]
y habita siempre[A7] en[D7] él;
[Am]concéde[A7]le el[D7] precio[G]so[C] don
